---
description: Ordering of xmlns / schemaLocation attributes on Block root elements
globs: "**/*.bml"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Block `xmlns` attribute order

On every `<block>` root, declare attributes in this order — nothing interleaved.

## 1. URIs and schemaLocation

```xml
xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                    "
```

Only HTTP(S) XML namespace URIs and `xsi:schemaLocation` belong here.

## 2. Package xmlns bindings

After the URI block, declare every `xmlns:<prefix>="<package.fqn>"` binding:

1. **BlockML packages** (`org.blockml.*`) first
2. **Domain packages** next — one group per domain root (e.g. all `com.machineblocks.*`, then any other domain)

Within each group, sort by package FQN (hierarchical / alphabetical).

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD — package before schemaLocation; BlockML and domain interleaved -->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:bml="org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:mbtype="com.machineblocks.bml.type"
  xmlns:unit="org.blockml.bml.unit"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.annotation.ScadAnnotation">

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:bml="org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:unit="org.blockml.bml.unit"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.annotation.ScadAnnotation"
  xmlns:mbtype="com.machineblocks.bml.type">
```
